e/14003089/assets/c32886c161e347daa9bf6fa7215f8a09abc4334632c33020c31ade6dfc4e7315.png)\n\nConsider the vector $v$ shown above. Find the vector $Av$ given that \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003089/state.json" "file_sha256" "0642b06331e49f39ba3507b0128498f7b8548369900c259748e072c00b6326f6"} {"question" "q-160624" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Consider the standard basis ${i,j}$ of the Euclidean plane ${R}^{2}$ and the unit square spanned by the vectors. Computing the images of ${i,j}$ under $A$, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{i}^{′} & =A(i)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=-i \\\\ {j}^{′} & =A(j)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=-j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we obtain the following diagram:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003089/assets/9fae3ec0ada3008937d88e4e76374a56da4369b1821cfee072c90d88b562df46.png)\n\nSo, the matrix represents a rotation of $\\pi $ radians (counterclockwise or clockwise) about the origin.\n\nTherefore, in order to find $Av$, we need to rotate $v$ (counterclockwise or clockwise) by an angle of $\\pi $ radians, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003089/assets/ed1a5e8a05ee0d9994d8ba90c02463fbf96525b1cd851bec685a005a34834f81.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003089/state.json" "file_sha256" "0642b06331e49f39ba3507b0128498f7b8548369900c259748e072c00b6326f6"} {"question" "q-160624" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003089/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d5412300abaf3d9cfe40c7fe60724db3bf41b03e257c8e1c9aa4b8a19eb15cd3"} {"question" "q-160624" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003089/state.json" "file_sha256" "0642b06331e49f39ba3507b0128498f7b8548369900c259748e072c00b6326f6"} {"question" "q-160624" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003089/assets/805c480c5341b6fbf3e8d5720187fead535db2a651939572a3a9faf453726087.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003089/assets/90dcf60e19c9031927df68a1d0be6b85c47910e6ec92e9052c292f667971d7f1.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003089/assets/9dc6d9d844c382cc5a8499929dfe7d3a9ab8bf59fc5b73b2cd4dab44c51e135f.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003089/assets/ba328088ca187ea28b241a302a486da1145a51c7e134d8d4f529f5f4a916ddc1.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003089/assets/c612d528e8fb432e4f63fdaae2649a4a41b0f3bed7751df5b5cc22074b57bb53.png"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003089/state.json" "file_sha256" "0642b06331e49f39ba3507b0128498f7b8548369900c259748e072c00b6326f6"} {"question" "q-160624" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003089/assets/9dc6d9d844c382cc5a8499929dfe7d3a9ab8bf59fc5b73b2cd4dab44c51e135f.png"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003089/state.json" "file_sha256" "0642b06331e49f39ba3507b0128498f7b8548369900c259748e072c00b6326f6"} {"question" "q-160647" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A triangle $S$ has vertices at  $(5,-1),(2,0),(-2,-1).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the **clockwise** rotation ${R}_{-\\pi /2}$ by an angle of $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ radians about the origin?\n\n- $(-1,-5)$\n- $(0,2)$\n- $(-1,-2)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003089/state.json" "file_sha256" "0642b06331e49f39ba3507b0128498f7b8548369900c259748e072c00b6326f6"} {"question" "q-160647" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The clockwise rotation ${R}_{-\\pi /2}$ by an angle of $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ radians is the same as counterclockwise rotation by an angle of $\\frac{3\\pi }{2}.$ It's given by the matrix\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the image of $S$ under the action of ${R}_{-\\pi /2},$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under ${R}_{-\\pi /2}$ by calculating the matrix product $RX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RX & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -5 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(-1,-5),(0,-2),(-1,2).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003089/state.json" "file_sha256" "0642b06331e49f39ba3507b0128498f7b8548369900c259748e072c00b6326f6"} {"question" "q-160647" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003089/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d5412300abaf3d9cfe40c7fe60724db3bf41b03e257c8e1c9aa4b8a19eb15cd3"} {"question" "q-160647" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003089/state.json" "file_sha256" "0642b06331e49f39ba3507b0128498f7b8548369900c259748e072c00b6326f6"} {"question" "q-160647" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003089/state.json" "file_sha256" "0642b06331e49f39ba3507b0128498f7b8548369900c259748e072c00b6326f6"} {"question" "q-160647" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003089/state.json" "file_sha256" "0642b06331e49f39ba3507b0128498f7b8548369900c259748e072c00b6326f6"}] "usage" {} "basis" 1082 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
